WEBVTT

00:02.010 --> 00:04.210
[Horse hooves cloping]

00:04.250 --> 00:06.650
[MOBLIT]
The report was right.

00:06.680 --> 00:09.250
The whole village
has been devastated.

00:09.280 --> 00:12.720
But there's not a drop of blood,
let alone any bodies.

00:12.750 --> 00:15.690
It's eerie. Still,
maybe they got out?

00:15.720 --> 00:17.090
It's not unheard of.

00:17.130 --> 00:19.160
In theory, I suppose.

00:19.190 --> 00:21.160
But then the question
becomes why Titans

00:21.200 --> 00:26.800
would smash up empty houses?
Bit difficult to believe.

00:26.840 --> 00:29.240
What's more, how far
were these people

00:29.270 --> 00:32.640
hoping to get by
leaving their horses here?

00:32.670 --> 00:34.070
That's a good point.

00:34.110 --> 00:36.540
So what do you think happened?

00:36.580 --> 00:39.550
Moblit, I found it! Look!

00:41.980 --> 00:44.050
There you are.

00:48.620 --> 00:51.790
[MALE SOLDIER 35B] You, uh...
you should see this.

00:53.200 --> 00:56.000
[MOBLIT] A portrait of Conny
Springer's parents, I presume?

00:56.030 --> 00:58.700
Seems very likely, sir.

00:58.730 --> 01:00.670
[MOBLIT and SOLDIERS gasp]

01:03.000 --> 01:04.040
It's alive!

01:04.070 --> 01:06.270
No! Stand down!

01:12.980 --> 01:14.850
[MOBLIT gasps]

01:19.920 --> 01:22.320
What the hell is going on?

01:22.690 --> 01:27.660
♪ Opening Song ♪

02:59.200 --> 03:01.340
[REINER] It's your call.
What's it gonna be?

03:01.370 --> 03:06.340
Is it Christa's future?
Or your own petty existence?

03:06.380 --> 03:10.280
Hey! Talk!
Who's the real enemy here?

03:10.320 --> 03:12.320
Tell me!

03:12.350 --> 03:14.450
[YMIR sighs]

03:14.490 --> 03:16.790
--Couldn't say.
--[EREN grunts]

03:16.860 --> 03:20.320
[REINER] All right, then.
Sorry, Eren.

03:22.160 --> 03:24.060
[Distant gunshot]

03:29.500 --> 03:31.070
[REINER]
You're kidding.

03:31.100 --> 03:34.440
[BERTHOLDT] The Scouts
are here? Already?

03:35.610 --> 03:37.310
Son of a bitch!

03:37.340 --> 03:39.980
Talk to me, Reiner.
What are you right now?

03:40.010 --> 03:42.210
A warrior. Calm down.

03:42.250 --> 03:45.310
Do you really think it's
wise for us to trust Ymir?

03:45.350 --> 03:48.280
Even though she's the one
who devoured Marcel?

03:48.320 --> 03:50.490
Sure. Don't you see?

03:50.520 --> 03:52.490
We have a handle
on her motives.

03:52.520 --> 03:55.120
When she turned human again,
odds are she just

03:55.160 --> 03:58.930
wandered around aimlessly only
giving a damn about herself.

03:58.960 --> 04:02.130
But then Christa
came into the picture.

04:02.170 --> 04:04.930
That's the kind of girl that
can change your whole world.

04:04.970 --> 04:07.300
We need her, and not
just because she's cute.

04:07.340 --> 04:08.570
The people she comes from

04:08.610 --> 04:11.340
are an important family
within the church.

04:11.380 --> 04:14.280
Plus, suppose Eren's
not the coordinate?

04:14.310 --> 04:16.980
Our job wouldn't be over.

04:17.020 --> 04:19.220
If it comes to that,
having Christa around

04:19.250 --> 04:22.350
will make the search
a lot easier.

04:22.390 --> 04:24.120
[Gasps]

04:27.130 --> 04:29.060
They're close.

04:29.090 --> 04:31.090
[EREN]
What are they talking about?

04:31.130 --> 04:35.060
They still plan on clearing out
before sundown or not?

04:35.100 --> 04:37.270
Please, let's just be done.

04:37.300 --> 04:39.470
The next time we come,
we'll take all three.

04:39.500 --> 04:43.240
Annie, Christa, and that.
It'll be clean and simple.

04:43.270 --> 04:45.580
Then we won't have
to come here anymore.

04:45.610 --> 04:49.380
Right. And we'll have
completed our damn mission.

04:49.410 --> 04:51.450
Just do me a favor, huh?

04:51.480 --> 04:54.980
Once we're home, try telling
Annie how you really feel.

04:55.020 --> 04:56.320
What's that
supposed to mean?

04:56.350 --> 04:58.150
Ugh. Come on.

04:58.190 --> 05:00.560
I've seen the way
you stare at her.

05:00.590 --> 05:02.190
I don't stare!

05:02.230 --> 05:04.590
Bertholdt, please,
life's short enough as it is.

05:04.630 --> 05:08.030
Just go for it. Besides,
you're both killers

05:08.070 --> 05:10.330
so she understands
where your head is.

05:15.670 --> 05:17.970
What're you two doing now?

05:18.010 --> 05:19.510
I thought we were
waiting till dark.

05:19.540 --> 05:22.250
There's been a slight
change of plans.

05:22.280 --> 05:25.620
I'm gonna ask you nicely not
to try to put up a fight.

05:30.190 --> 05:33.620
Easy. There's no need
for us to get all violent.

05:33.660 --> 05:36.190
It's not like I can
resist like this.

05:36.230 --> 05:41.230
I mean, take a look at me.
Just, calm down, okay?

05:45.300 --> 05:49.370
[EREN grunts]

05:49.410 --> 05:53.110
Die! Die! Die! Die!
Die, you evil--!

05:53.140 --> 05:55.440
[REINER grunts]

05:55.480 --> 05:59.020
[REINER and EREN grunting]

05:59.050 --> 06:01.750
Bastard! I'll--I'll kill you!

06:01.790 --> 06:03.650
I'll rip you apart!

06:03.690 --> 06:07.320
Explain to me
why we're leaving early.

06:07.360 --> 06:10.760
Ymir. When you changed
back into a human,

06:10.800 --> 06:13.360
d'you have any memory
of the person you ate?

06:13.400 --> 06:15.430
[Gasps]

06:15.470 --> 06:20.470
Huh. No, not really.

06:20.510 --> 06:24.640
We're talking about something
that happened five years ago.

06:24.680 --> 06:26.580
But the way you're asking,
I'm guessing that

06:26.610 --> 06:28.540
it was someone you knew?

06:28.580 --> 06:33.580
[EREN yelling, groaning]

06:33.620 --> 06:38.590
I see. Then I'm, uh,
sorry for not remembering.

06:38.620 --> 06:42.390
[Yelling]

06:43.630 --> 06:46.660
Hey, it's not your
fault that you don't.

06:46.700 --> 06:49.400
It was the same
for Reiner and me.

06:49.430 --> 06:51.400
[YMIR]
Yeah?

06:51.440 --> 06:53.670
[BERTHOLDT] Eren doesn't
remember either.

06:53.710 --> 06:56.510
[YMIR]
Is that how it works?

06:58.640 --> 07:01.040
You hold that against me?

07:01.080 --> 07:06.180
I don't think so.
I mean. I don't know.

07:06.220 --> 07:09.650
Suppose I have to believe you
didn't want to eat anyone.

07:09.690 --> 07:14.090
How, uh, how long were you
wandering outside the walls?

07:14.130 --> 07:18.430
Oh, about sixty years.
Hell on earth.

07:18.460 --> 07:22.100
Every day was like
waking up into a nightmare.

07:23.130 --> 07:24.630
[Gunshot]

07:31.780 --> 07:34.140
Red smoke signal, sir.

07:38.480 --> 07:40.280
The hell?

07:40.320 --> 07:43.590
[Gasps]

07:43.620 --> 07:45.650
Commander Erwin,
we're surrounded!

07:45.690 --> 07:50.190
There is a way around.
Should we head towards it?

07:50.230 --> 07:54.130
[ERWIN] No. We don't
have time for a detour.

07:54.170 --> 07:58.470
We'll forge ahead!
Soldiers! Prepare to fight!

08:00.570 --> 08:03.440
[REINER] For now, we find
a place without Titans!

08:03.470 --> 08:06.280
As far away as possible!

08:06.310 --> 08:08.780
I haven't recovered enough
to outrun these guys.

08:08.810 --> 08:10.580
They surround us,
there's jack shit

08:10.620 --> 08:12.350
my Titan form
can do right now.

08:12.380 --> 08:13.620
Then why the hell
didn't we just wait

08:13.650 --> 08:15.320
for the sun to go down?

08:15.350 --> 08:16.620
[Gasps]

08:16.650 --> 08:19.790
Smoke signals? Did the
Scouts come to save us?

08:19.820 --> 08:21.560
Damn it. That formation
wouldn't work

08:21.590 --> 08:24.490
unless they hoisted a bunch
of horses over the wall.

08:24.530 --> 08:26.860
Who gave that order?

08:26.900 --> 08:29.400
I honestly thought we had
more time than this.

08:29.470 --> 08:31.500
It's gotta be Commander Erwin.

08:31.540 --> 08:33.170
Hard as nails, that one.

08:33.200 --> 08:34.700
[Distant gunshot]

08:35.470 --> 08:38.470
[REINER] Damn.
They're already that close?

08:38.510 --> 08:41.140
It's Eren's fault
for losing his cool.

08:44.920 --> 08:48.350
[YMIR]
Wait. Is she...?

08:50.920 --> 08:52.720
Christa's here.

08:52.760 --> 08:55.460
Reiner! We have
to go back! Now!

08:55.490 --> 08:56.760
Christa's with them!

08:56.790 --> 08:58.830
--What?
--This is our best chance!

08:58.860 --> 09:01.260
You're full of it!
No way you can see that far!

09:01.300 --> 09:03.730
Look, I just know!
Think about it, okay?

09:03.770 --> 09:05.600
She's a big softie, right?

09:05.640 --> 09:09.370
Stupid girl's come
to rescue me! She had to!

09:09.410 --> 09:11.340
Yeah, well so what?

09:11.380 --> 09:13.780
I'm sorry!
It'll have to wait!

09:13.810 --> 09:14.880
[YMIR]
What?

09:14.910 --> 09:17.850
We can't grab her
the way things are now!

09:17.880 --> 09:20.620
There's no way to
bust up that formation!

09:20.650 --> 09:22.550
Another time!

09:22.590 --> 09:24.390
How long you want me to wait?

09:24.420 --> 09:26.520
Maybe I should just hold off
on that until I've been

09:26.560 --> 09:28.720
gobbled up by one of
your warrior pals?

09:28.760 --> 09:30.790
Oh no! I don't think so!

09:30.830 --> 09:32.630
Don't be that way!

09:32.660 --> 09:34.930
Nobody's trying to
trick you, I swear it!

09:34.970 --> 09:36.400
[YMIR]
Prove it, then!

09:36.430 --> 09:38.530
There's no time like
the present, asshole!

09:38.570 --> 09:41.340
Damn you! Get down there
and bring her with us!

09:41.370 --> 09:43.310
I need to see her!

09:45.280 --> 09:46.510
You don't understand.

09:46.740 --> 09:50.650
The way things are going,
will.

09:59.489 --> 10:01.075
[BERTHOLDT]
We can't.

10:03.348 --> 10:05.018
Let it go, Ymir.

10:07.588 --> 10:09.018
Who knows whether
we'll even manage

10:09.048 --> 10:12.618
to survive this. Sorry.
It's just too risky.

10:12.658 --> 10:15.788
Listen to me.
You have my word.

10:15.828 --> 10:18.215
I want her out of this
as much as you do.

10:18.628 --> 10:21.883
Bear with me.
You have to trust us!

10:23.098 --> 10:25.438
This is what's best
for Christa!

10:25.468 --> 10:27.338
Do you understand?

10:28.808 --> 10:32.031
Yes, I understand.
Real question is, do you?

10:33.048 --> 10:34.000
Of course!

10:35.348 --> 10:36.778
All right, then.

10:36.818 --> 10:38.618
Thank you for that.

10:40.148 --> 10:44.412
[YMIR] It's happening again.
I've come so far.

10:44.718 --> 10:50.958
Done so much. And still wound up
falling for my own bullshit.

10:50.998 --> 10:53.898
[MAN 35A]
Well. They look promising.

11:02.878 --> 11:04.508
[MAN 35A]
What about this one?

11:04.538 --> 11:06.508
[MAN 35B]
Mm.

11:06.548 --> 11:08.008
[MAN 35A]
Hello there.

11:08.048 --> 11:10.198
How would you feel about
coming to live with us?

11:10.948 --> 11:12.948
Think of it as the start
of a brand-new life.

11:14.718 --> 11:18.988
Of course, a brand-new life
needs a brand-new name.

11:19.018 --> 11:20.788
Don't you agree?

11:20.828 --> 11:22.428
[YMIR]
Huh?

11:22.458 --> 11:26.658
[YMIR] That day... That was the
first time I lied to myself.

11:26.698 --> 11:29.168
Told myself I had
no say in the matter.

11:29.198 --> 11:32.798
That I never
had a choice. But...

11:33.838 --> 11:36.868
[MAN 35A] It is this Lady Ymir
that inherits the blood

11:36.908 --> 11:40.508
of His Majesty the king.
So long as she graces us

11:40.548 --> 11:44.618
with her presence,
immortality shall be ours.

11:44.648 --> 11:49.188
[Clapping]

11:49.218 --> 11:52.958
[YMIR] To be fair,
it wasn't all that bad.

11:52.988 --> 11:54.758
[Gasps]

11:54.788 --> 12:00.458
[YMIR] My food wasn't cold.
I no longer slept in the dirt.

12:00.498 --> 12:02.168
[SISTER]
Lady Ymir.

12:02.198 --> 12:05.938
[YMIR] Best of all, I knew what
it meant to feel needed.

12:05.968 --> 12:07.598
For the first time in my life,

12:07.638 --> 12:10.708
I actually meant something
to someone else.

12:10.738 --> 12:14.808
That, by far, was more
precious than anything.

12:14.848 --> 12:17.608
Then, one day...

12:17.648 --> 12:22.148
[BELIEVERS holler]

12:22.188 --> 12:25.088
[MAN 35A] It's her fault!
The girl's to blame!

12:25.118 --> 12:27.888
She said the blood of the king
flowed in her veins!

12:27.928 --> 12:31.058
We're only guilty
of believing her!

12:31.098 --> 12:33.698
[YMIR] I was cruelly
reminded that everything

12:33.728 --> 12:37.450
I clung to was an act.

12:38.198 --> 12:40.238
Is that so?

12:40.268 --> 12:42.968
I-I only...

12:53.518 --> 12:56.748
It's true.

12:56.788 --> 12:58.558
I am Ymir!

12:58.588 --> 13:01.118
The king's blood
runs through me!

13:01.158 --> 13:02.888
[BELIEVERS gasp]

13:02.928 --> 13:06.258
[YMIR] Lie once,
the rest follow easy.

13:06.298 --> 13:07.798
[YMIR gasps]

13:07.828 --> 13:11.568
If it saved
their necks, so be it.

13:11.598 --> 13:16.508
Trouble was, things didn't
quite work out that way.

13:18.808 --> 13:20.738
[Breathe rapidly]

13:20.778 --> 13:23.148
[Screams]
Help me!

13:23.178 --> 13:26.278
[Coughs and screams]

13:28.818 --> 13:33.088
Stop this! I'm begging you!
It's not right!

13:33.128 --> 13:34.758
[Squelch]

13:34.788 --> 13:36.288
[YMIR yelps]

13:39.798 --> 13:44.268
[YMIR] That's when I realized.
I'd had it coming all along.

13:46.138 --> 13:49.038
I'd deceived
those gullible bastards,

13:49.068 --> 13:51.818
but that wasn't what I was
being punished for really.

13:52.878 --> 13:55.578
It was for deceiving myself

13:55.608 --> 13:58.318
into thinking
someone needed me.

13:58.348 --> 14:01.048
What else did I expect?

14:01.088 --> 14:04.918
That's what comes of looking
at the world through a veil.

14:11.728 --> 14:13.628
[YMIR TITAN growls]

14:14.128 --> 14:15.298
[ALL gasp]

14:15.328 --> 14:18.068
[MARCEL]
Titan! Run!

14:19.138 --> 14:21.608
[MARCEL grunts]

14:24.138 --> 14:28.708
[MARCEL hollers]

14:28.748 --> 14:30.078
No!

14:30.118 --> 14:32.148
[Screams]

14:40.988 --> 14:42.658
[YMIR gasps]

14:55.268 --> 14:56.868
[YMIR]
When I opened my eyes,

14:57.908 --> 15:00.200
the first thing
I saw was freedom.

15:02.148 --> 15:04.278
The first thing I thought

15:04.318 --> 15:06.218
was if there's
such thing as fate,

15:06.248 --> 15:08.248
she's a fickle little whore.

15:08.318 --> 15:10.288
[Laughs]

15:10.318 --> 15:12.168
Right then and there

15:13.258 --> 15:15.758
I made a vow.

15:15.788 --> 15:18.000
No more deceiving myself.

15:19.668 --> 15:22.487
No more falling
for my own line.

15:24.068 --> 15:26.938
From then on, I'd be real.

15:29.978 --> 15:32.308
[MALE ORDER OF THE WALLS 35A]
So, how did that play out?

15:32.338 --> 15:33.838
[MALE ORDER OF THE WALLS 35B]
Ah, the child was given

15:33.878 --> 15:35.308
the name "Christa Lenz."

15:35.348 --> 15:37.778
Then, she was packed off
to the Cadet Corps.

15:37.818 --> 15:39.218
That is a pity.

15:39.248 --> 15:42.848
Poor wretch. Would've been
better were she never born.

15:44.688 --> 15:46.358
Are you trying
to pick a fight?

15:46.388 --> 15:50.088
All right, sure.
Makes no difference to me.

15:54.998 --> 15:56.698
[YMIR]
And then...

15:57.938 --> 15:59.338
What do we have here?

15:59.368 --> 16:01.738
This your idea
of trying to be nice?

16:01.768 --> 16:03.108
[BOTH gasp]

16:03.138 --> 16:04.000
Well, uh.

16:05.278 --> 16:06.490
[YMIR]
And then I met you.

16:09.008 --> 16:11.678
Immediately, I could tell.

16:11.718 --> 16:13.330
You and I were the same.

16:14.018 --> 16:17.118
You nourished yourself on lies.

16:17.158 --> 16:19.788
Together, we give our hearts!

16:20.888 --> 16:22.788
[CADETS]
Sir!

16:22.828 --> 16:24.288
[YMIR] Here was someone
desperately trying

16:24.328 --> 16:27.750
to convince herself of
something she knew wasn't true.

16:27.998 --> 16:31.838
I get it. Believe me.

16:31.868 --> 16:32.478
And don't worry.

16:33.438 --> 16:37.220
I'm not asking you
to understand.

16:37.438 --> 16:42.208
No. What I want
is very simple.

16:42.248 --> 16:46.048
Just let me be honest
with myself one last time.

16:46.078 --> 16:47.878
That's all.

16:49.788 --> 16:50.948
Let's face it, guys.

16:50.988 --> 16:53.018
I'm the one
best suited for this.

16:53.058 --> 16:57.358
[BERTHOLDT hollers]

16:57.398 --> 16:58.898
What are you doing?

16:58.928 --> 17:01.328
Hey, shut the hell up and
use your head for a second.

17:01.368 --> 17:05.238
In a forest like this I'm the
one who can shine. Right?

17:05.268 --> 17:07.098
[Yells]

17:12.978 --> 17:15.378
[BERTHOLDT] Ymir!
Knock it off! We'll fall!

17:15.408 --> 17:17.208
Do you think
that I give a damn?

17:17.248 --> 17:19.348
I have the advantage.

17:19.378 --> 17:21.988
Any other time you two
would outclass me.

17:22.018 --> 17:24.788
But my Titan form's more agile.

17:24.818 --> 17:26.918
I could leap through
the trees, grab Eren,

17:26.958 --> 17:29.758
and rendezvous with the Scouts
before you knew what hit you.

17:29.798 --> 17:31.998
Wouldn't be that hard.

17:34.168 --> 17:36.168
Either you agree to take
Christa with us today,

17:36.198 --> 17:38.098
right now, or so
help me I will throw

17:38.138 --> 17:39.798
your whole plan out of whack!

17:39.838 --> 17:41.908
Uh! Are you
completely insane?

17:41.938 --> 17:43.068
That doesn't help her!

17:43.108 --> 17:45.038
I thought that
you genuinely cared!

17:45.078 --> 17:47.878
I do. In my way.

17:47.908 --> 17:50.848
If it robs her of a future,
then life's a bitch,

17:50.878 --> 17:54.118
but by god I will live
to see her again!

17:54.148 --> 17:57.248
I've made my peace with
what that says about me.

17:57.288 --> 18:00.018
You guys have no idea
what it's like.

18:00.058 --> 18:02.158
She knows what
a shitty person I am,

18:02.228 --> 18:06.128
but she still
smiles at me. I can't--

18:06.158 --> 18:07.298
Damn it.

18:07.328 --> 18:10.998
[YMIR] Don't be pissed.
I have a fairly decent plan.

18:11.038 --> 18:12.798
Besides, if I stay and fight,

18:12.838 --> 18:15.408
it'll be easier
for you three to get away.

18:15.438 --> 18:18.208
Then again,
if you don't like it,

18:18.278 --> 18:22.308
we can always tear each other
apart like animals!

18:24.818 --> 18:29.588
[SOLDIERS screaming]

18:32.288 --> 18:35.188
[Gasps]
That light.

18:35.228 --> 18:36.558
You saw it, too, huh?

18:36.598 --> 18:38.258
It's coming from the forest!

18:38.298 --> 18:41.258
I think someone's
transforming into a Titan!

18:41.298 --> 18:45.098
We're out of time.
Soldiers, disperse!

18:45.138 --> 18:47.498
The enemy has
assumed Titan form!

18:47.538 --> 18:50.368
Find Eren and
get him out of there!

18:52.008 --> 18:53.038
[SOLDIERS gasp]

18:53.078 --> 18:57.008
[Screams]

19:00.188 --> 19:01.518
Another MP.

19:01.548 --> 19:03.388
[ERWIN]
Battle is not our objective!

19:03.458 --> 19:07.058
Locate, recover, and retreat!

19:07.088 --> 19:08.488
Round up the horses!

19:08.528 --> 19:10.228
Right away, sir!

19:14.468 --> 19:16.298
[HANNES] First thing we do
is pinpoint the enemy

19:16.338 --> 19:17.528
and tell the others!

19:17.568 --> 19:21.908
They're fleeing through the
woods, so stay sharp! Break!

19:21.938 --> 19:23.968
--[MIKASA] Eren.
--[ARMIN] Where are you?

19:24.008 --> 19:27.338
[YMIR TITAN roars]

19:29.008 --> 19:31.008
That's the
scream of a Titan!

19:31.048 --> 19:33.178
It came from just up ahead!

19:39.188 --> 19:40.418
I can see you!

19:40.458 --> 19:43.228
No, wait a second!

19:43.258 --> 19:45.628
It's actually Ymir!
This is her Titan form.

19:45.658 --> 19:48.328
She's one of
the people they took!

19:48.368 --> 19:49.968
What the hell happened?

19:49.998 --> 19:54.168
Where is everybody else?
Is Eren okay?

19:54.208 --> 19:57.168
What about
Bertholdt and Reiner?

19:59.408 --> 20:01.078
So this is Ymir.

20:01.108 --> 20:02.508
Did she assume
Titan form to take on

20:02.548 --> 20:04.048
Reiner and escape?

20:04.078 --> 20:05.278
Ymir! What's the deal?

20:05.318 --> 20:06.948
Did you manage
to get away from them?

20:06.988 --> 20:08.388
What direction did they go?

20:08.418 --> 20:12.418
Give us something
to go on! Anything!

20:12.458 --> 20:14.388
[CONNY]
Say something already!

20:14.428 --> 20:17.658
Come on, ugly!
We're kinda in a rush!

20:19.128 --> 20:21.298
Is she keeping
an eye out for Reiner?

20:21.328 --> 20:24.068
[Gasps]

20:24.098 --> 20:26.068
Something isn't right.

20:26.098 --> 20:29.568
Why--Why is she
looking at us one by one?

20:29.608 --> 20:32.378
[CHRISTA]
Ymir!

20:32.408 --> 20:33.608
There you are!

20:33.648 --> 20:36.348
Thank goodness
you're all right!

20:41.618 --> 20:43.418
[BOTH gasp]

20:43.458 --> 20:44.988
What?

20:45.018 --> 20:47.958
Did she just--?
Ymir, what are you doing?

20:51.158 --> 20:54.358
Don't just stand there!
Move your asses!

20:58.168 --> 21:00.298
[JEAN] She's fast!
We're losing her!

21:00.338 --> 21:01.638
Why would she do that?

21:01.668 --> 21:03.268
What's wrong with you people?

21:03.308 --> 21:06.308
Am I seriously the only one
who saw this coming?

21:06.338 --> 21:08.648
Well, it's clear where
her loyalties are now!

21:08.678 --> 21:11.278
She and Reiner
are on the same side!

21:11.318 --> 21:13.618
We were lured into a trap!

21:15.218 --> 21:16.948
[BERTHOLDT]
Heads up. She's back.

21:16.988 --> 21:18.418
Good.

21:43.578 --> 21:45.248
Oh, no!

21:46.648 --> 21:49.988
[ARMIN] No! They're getting
away with Eren!

21:51.518 --> 21:55.258
[HANNES] Move it!
Get on your damn horses!

22:02.098 --> 22:04.728
This ain't over, you hear me?

22:04.768 --> 22:07.638
I'll get him back
if it costs me my life!

22:10.708 --> 22:15.678
♪ Closing Song ♪
